# Safe production deploy (VLESS / Reality)

Public HTTPS path (camouflage):

```text
Client :443 → xray (VLESS Reality) → dest 127.0.0.1:8443 → host nginx → 127.0.0.1:18080
```

VLESS clients use Reality; ordinary browsers hitting the same `:443` with site SNI get the **real host** via fallthrough. That dest **must** stay `127.0.0.1:8443`.

## Hard rules

1. App deploys must **not** edit Reality keys / shortIds / privateKey. Allowed only when the user explicitly asks to **fix Reality/VLESS/camouflage**.
2. **Never** `docker compose down`, stop host `nginx`, or bind product containers to `:443` / `:8443`.
3. Prod web stays on **loopback** `127.0.0.1:18080`. Ops stays on loopback `8001` / `5174`.
4. Rolling `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up --build -d` only.
5. **Always** run `scripts/assert-edge-safe.sh` before compose up. On the VPS use `STRICT_HOST=1`.
6. After deploy, local Reality fallthrough (`--resolve host:443:127.0.0.1`) must return 200. Prefer that over flaky public `:8443` probes from some ISPs.
7. If fallthrough is down while nginx `:8443` is up → run `scripts/reality-guard.sh` (rate-limited xray restart). Do not “fix” by redeploying the app.
8. New public hostnames need nginx on `:8443` **and** Reality `serverNames` (only when fixing edge / user asked).
9. Never print xray UUIDs, private keys, shortIds, or full Reality config in chat.
10. Keep `reality-guard.timer` enabled on the VPS; do not disable it during routine deploys.

## Programmatic fuses

| Fuse | Role |
|------|------|
| `scripts/assert-edge-safe.sh` | Refuses bad compose ports; on host checks owners + Reality dest + fallthrough |
| `scripts/reality-guard.sh` | Restarts xray only when `:8443` OK and local `:443` fallthrough fails (budget/hour) |
| `scripts/deploy.sh` | Calls both; may trigger one guard restart post-deploy |
| systemd `xray` After=`nginx` | Camouflage backend must exist before Reality listens |
| `reality-guard.timer` | Periodic fuse |

## Post-deploy (no secrets)

```bash
STRICT_HOST=1 ./scripts/assert-edge-safe.sh
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "443=%{http_code}\n" --max-time 15 https://aichallenge.arcilite.ru/
```
